 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-161", "title": "The suite is not robust to a relative PATH entry: tests that spawn sys.executable into a scratch cwd die before asserting", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ecbbd8b9a81caf89c7d304fb6e601d39f70482dcaa9cf6fd2d773e55d137a0c5"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-09 by the AUG-127 judge (.gitreins/history/2026-11-09/d2447397/verdict.json): with PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH, sys.executable itself is the RELATIVE string '.venv/bin/python3'; tests/test_spec_repository_root.py::run_auger spawns it with cwd set to a scratch consumer repo, so argv[0] resolves against the wrong directory and 6 of 9 tests errored with FileNotFoundError before any assertion ran (anchored: 'assert 1 == 0', '2 failed in 0.19s'). Fixed for that ONE file in 1841d79 (os.path.abspath). Not yet swept: other test files spawn sys.executable too (grep sys.executable tests/*.py = 18 sites) and any site that also sets cwd to a scratch dir has the same latent failure; a green gate never shows it because the gate's PATH is absolute.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a written audit enumerates every sys.executable subprocess spawn in tests/ whose call sets cwd=<scratch dir> and shows each is either absolute-resolved or proven unaffected (inherited cwd). PASS: PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_spec_repository_root.py exits 0 with '9 passed' (the fixed instance stays green). PASS: with the audit's fixes applied, PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q <the audited files> exits 0 and reproduces the absolute-PATH pass count for the same selections.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:18:30.258149+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-09T09:18:30.258149+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-162", "title": "The live JEV arm reds the whole 15-minute gate on a transient JEV miss: the -1 sentinel is stamped with a real jev_checked_at and the test asserts a numeric verdict", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2ea91887c141e4bdcf547c664d32d162a3b3f0e959691ea62a8138f891111a3e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "6c8f88b2", "ts": "2026-11-10T12:17:32.593159+00:00"}]}, "evidence_run_id": "6c8f88b2", "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-10 on ONE unchanged tree (main a0bd6b1, 717-test gate): the live JEV arm tests/test_auger.py::test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question reds the ENTIRE 15-minute gate whenever the JEV call misses, which makes every GitReins verdict in this repo intermittently unpayable. Evidence: tier1 red in run efd20b1d (05:40:48Z) and again in run e77575d1 (06:31Z) with the identical assertion \"assert q[\\\"jev_checked_at\\\"] and q[\\\"jev_already_answered\\\"] >= 0\" -> \"assert (2026-11-10T06:31:12.560236+00:00 and -1 >= 0)\"; the SAME test passed in-suite on the same tree at 03:03Z (verdict 5c0158a1, 717 passed) and passed ALONE twice at the same head (21.30s, 23.57s). Mechanism: auger.jev() returns (None, \"all N JEV keys failed; last: ...\") on any transport/upstream miss, record_followup() then stamps the documented unknown sentinel jev_already_answered=-1 (auger.py:3389) together with a real jev_checked_at, and the test asserts a NUMERIC verdict (tests/test_auger.py:8321) even though its own docstring says the contract is \"the decision was drilled and the row was stored - never that a model agreed with a plan\". So a third-party hiccup is indistinguishable from a code regression and costs a full 20-minute judge run. Independent lane check this tick: the JEV endpoint answered HTTP 400 to a deliberately malformed probe body (i.e. the keys authenticate and the host is reachable), and one of the 6 discovered OpenRouter keys answers 401 \"User not found\" - a dead key in the rotation adds a failed attempt per call.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a question the gate never examined carries NO check stamp: with `auger.recall` forced to return no hits, `feedback --budget 1` stores the follow-up row with `jev_checked_at == \"\"` and `jev_already_answered == -1.0`, spends ZERO JEV calls, and prints the `not gated ... no JEV verdict was produced` line. Falsifier: at 425c846 the same run stamps a real `jev_checked_at` beside `-1` and prints no such line (measured: the new test is RED against HEAD's auger.py, GREEN with the fix). PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"no_evidence_could_answer\"\nPASS: a JEV outage stays fail-closed AND is classifiable as a loud skip: with the gate forced to return (None, \"\", \"\", \"all 6 JEV keys failed; last: HTTP 401 User not found\"), `feedback --budget 1` exits 1, stores no follow-up, and prints `WARNING gate unavailable` naming the JEV failure; the live arm's `live_unavailable_reason(out)` returns a skip reason naming JEV+401 for that output and \"\" for an ordinary transcript (so a skip can never mask a real regression). PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"jev_unavailable\"\nPASS: the live arm requires the two gate columns to AGREE instead of requiring a model verdict: `tests/test_auger.py::test_feedback_live_proposes_gates_and_asks_a_real_question` asserts `bool(q[\"jev_checked_at\"]) == (q[\"jev_already_answered\"] >= 0)` and still asserts the row exists, is trackable (`opens` edge to D-002), and matches its status branch (satisfies edge or askable). Falsifier: the old `q[\"jev_checked_at\"] and q[\"jev_already_answered\"] >= 0` reds on a healthy tree whenever the gate answers without a model call. PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -rs tests/test_auger.py -k \"feedback_live\"\nPASS: the answered path keeps its positive assertion in a DISTINCT test (the fix cannot be \"delete the assertion\"): `test_feedback_turns_a_thin_decision_into_a_named_followup` still requires a numeric noul (0.10) together with a stamped check, and `propagate` no longer writes a sentinel verdict for a question it did not gate. PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_auger.py -k \"feedback or jev or propagate\" (28 passed measured on the fixed tree)\nPASS: the whole gate is green on the MERGED main tree: bash tests/gate.sh with PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin first, DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000, DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY from ~/.duckbrain/foreman-status.token and AUGER_GATE_PYTEST_BUDGET=3000s exits 0, so a GitReins verdict in this repo is payable again. PROOF: gate transcript recorded in the goal's evidence (worktree run + post-merge main run)", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-10T06:44:11.663752+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:17:32.593159+00:00", "foreman_note": "PREMISE CORRECTED 2026-11-10 (driver): the row's stated mechanism was only half right. Measured in code: feedback stamps g['checked_at'] = now() UNCONDITIONALLY before record_followup (auger.py:3559) and propagate patches jev_checked_at unconditionally (auger.py:2895), so the -1 sentinel lands beside a real timestamp whenever the gate answers WITHOUT a model call — gate_question returns (None,'','',None) on empty recall and on the AUG-063 cosine-miss shortcut. In the two observed reds the CLI printed 'proposed: 1' and exited 0 with a question stored, which cannot happen on the gate_error path (that path exits 1 and stores nothing), so the reds were the NO-CALL path, not a transport outage. Consequence is worse than the flake: propagate skips re-gating any question with jev_checked_at set, so a question nobody gated was never gated again. Fix: stamp only with a verdict (feedback + propagate), keep the JEV-outage path fail-closed with its WARNING, print a distinct 'not gated ... no JEV verdict was produced' line, and let the live arm skip ONLY on the CLI's own outage diagnostic. Criteria rewritten with the measured falsifier (new test RED at 425c846, GREEN with the fix).\n\nIMPLEMENTATION LANDED 2026-11-10 on main 6b77fc1 (ff-merge of wt/auger-xml-hardening after rebase onto 425c846). Fix: checked_at travels only with a verdict (feedback auger.py:3567); propagate skips the write outright when the gate produced no verdict (auger.py:2893) instead of stamping a sentinel that permanently suppressed re-gating; `auger feedback` prints a distinct 'not gated ... no JEV verdict was produced' line; live arm asserts the two columns AGREE and skips loudly only on the CLI's own outage diagnostic (live_unavailable_reason, with a control). Two deterministic falsifiers added; the no-evidence one is RED against 425c846's auger.py and GREEN here. Evidence: worktree gate GATE PASS rc 0 (712 passed/2 skipped, 891.61s, /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-aug162-gate.log); merged-main gate GATE PASS rc 0 (719 passed/2 skipped, 884.82s, /home/kara/.hermes/goals/auger-aug162-gate-main.log); ruff format+check clean. Row stays in_progress: no GitReins verdict yet, and --status complete needs a real evidence_run_id. NEXT: gitreins judge AUG-162 at 6b77fc1 (task id == row id), then re-judge AUG-133 on the now-payable gate.\n\nJUDGED PASS 2026-11-10 12:16Z — task AUG-162 graded at head 9725360 (contains the fix 6b77fc1; git diff --stat 6b77fc1..HEAD is board-only). tier1 PASS: lint (scanners), secrets (gitleaks clean + builtin 251 files clean), tests GATE PASS with LIVE ARMS ran 2 / skipped 0 — the inherited live-JEV flake that red-ed two earlier judges is gone on this tree. tier2 PASS COMPLETE 8/8 items (5 authored + 3 derived, incl. \"skip is narrow / cannot mask a regression\" and \"not gated line does not fire on a real verdict\"). Verdict artifact .gitreins/history/2026-11-10/6c8f88b2/verdict.json (CLI printed hex 8235e2ec — bound by the directory whose task_id+commit match, not the printed hex). Caps: GITREINS_MAX_ITERATIONS=400 GITREINS_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=8M, AUGER_GATE_PYTEST_BUDGET=3000s on the gate-form venv. Direct gates re-executed verbatim before task create (4 pytest selectors green at 9725360). CI at the judged head: run 42792032470 success.", "capability_tags": ["python", "tests", "live-substrate"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "97253601ea20175e5395c16bc12cecb49a18686d", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-163", "title": "tests/test_xml_task_contract.py SKIPS its boardctl arms when boardctl is off PATH, so the gate can go green with the export/refusal surface unexecuted", "detail": {"fingerprint": "97a3318a5a9b2189cc6fa8221c05a51cc5eaa0611c3270cfa7c2f9ce373d12b6"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-11 (verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/2b6d77d6, task AUG-121, commit 8314316): the AC3/AC4/AC6 proofs were run under PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin, which omits /home/kara/.local/bin where boardctl lives. Result: 3 skipped, 8 passed, rc 0 for the whole file. The tests raise pytest.skip at tests/test_xml_task_contract.py:393 when shutil.which(\"boardctl\") is None, so the approved-plan boardctl export, the stale-digest byte-identical refusal and the only-create/readback surface scan never executed. The repo gate does not distinguish that from a pass. This is the same defect class the repo gate fixed for its own arms (AUG-130: a skipped arm is not a passed arm) but it survives inside a test file: any CI or consumer environment without boardctl gets a green suite covering nothing on this surface. Fix direction: make the dependency a hard failure (pytest.fail with the resolved PATH printed) rather than a skip, or have the enclosing gate arm assert the collected-vs-run count for this file.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1. A proof run of tests/test_xml_task_contract.py under a PATH with NO boardctl must FAIL (exit 0 with skips is the defect): PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_xml_task_contract.py; expected: rc != 0 and the output names the missing boardctl requirement. FAILIF: rc 0, or 3 skipped with 8 passed.\n2. The same file under the full proof PATH must still pass 11 tests: PROOF: cd /home/kara/auger && PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:/home/kara/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_xml_task_contract.py; expected: 11 passed. FAILIF: any skip or failure.\n3. tests/gate.sh must not be able to report GATE PASS while these three obligations skipped: PROOF: grep -n 'test_xml_task_contract' tests/gate.sh plus a run of the arm under the boardctl-less PATH showing a non-zero gate verdict (or a hard error naming boardctl). FAILIF: the gate exits 0 with the obligations skipped.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T09:56:08.590561+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T09:56:08.590561+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["tests", "gate", "boardctl", "xml"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
-{"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-164", "title": "the coverage gate marks a 9/9-PASS verdict FAILED when the evaluator elides a long token inside its criterion echo", "detail": {"fingerprint": "4896e1de3b5e533e4ca9cccc8454ca26864c0a2d1871d1090bb866911e31cfd6"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-11 (driver tick, auger XML goal). Judge run .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json graded gitreins task AUG-121 at commit ab10427290d8 with NINE items, every one status=PASS (six authored ACs each ran its exact proof command: 1 passed / 5 passed / 1 passed / 1 passed / 1 passed / 2 passed, no skips, boardctl present on the proof PATH; three derived items also PASS), tier1 lint+secrets+tests PASS (real bash tests/gate.sh) — and the verdict still persisted passed=false because the coverage gate reported 'Coverage FAILED — ungraded' listing all six authored criteria.\n\nMECHANISM (engine/gate.py:241 check_coverage + :180 _matches): each criterion is matched against items[].criterion by exact normalized text, then by a bidirectional prefix rule. The evaluator echoed each criterion with its long PATH literal elided to '...' ('PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:/home/kara/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin' -> 'PATH=...'), so every item's criterion text differs mid-string, not at a boundary; measured SequenceMatcher ratios per criterion: 0.9072, 0.9472, 0.9293, 0.9007, 0.9105, 0.9255. Exact match fails, prefix match fails (the divergence is interior), so all six are 'ungraded' although their items are PASS.\n\nNOT A CRITERIA DEFECT: three sibling verdicts on the same day (dd902d09 AUG-119, 35a8093c AUG-118, a9b1feeb AUG-150) matched at ratio 1.000 with equally long commands, so this is evaluator echo variance colliding with a matcher that has no interior-insensitive comparison — a 9/9-PASS verdict reported as a failure.\n\nIMPACT: any row whose criteria carry a long literal token (absolute PATH, long node-id list) can lose a genuine PASS to this, and the row then stays open while the work is verifiably done (AUG-121 was re-armed with a compact $PWD/$HOME PATH form as the workaround). Fix belongs in gitreins engine/gate.py, not in auger.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1. PASS: the recorded verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json (task AUG-121, commit ab10427290d8, 9 items whose status is PASS for all nine) must make engine.gate.verdict_is_passing return True; reproduce with PYTHONPATH=<gitreins site-packages> python3 -c 'import json;from engine.gate import check_coverage as cc, verdict_is_passing as vp;v=json.load(open(\".gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json\"));c=cc(v,v[\"task_criteria\"]);print(len(c.graded),len(c.ungraded),vp(v,v[\"task_criteria\"]))' -> pre-fix prints 0 6 False; post-fix must print 6 0 True.\n2. PASS: the fix is not 'always pass': a temp copy of that verdict with items[2].status set to FAIL must yield check_coverage(...).failing == 1 and verdict_is_passing False (one-field mutation, printed counts).\n3. PASS: matching stays strict: an item whose criterion text is truncated to its first 30 characters must still be ungraded (fixture prints ungraded == 1), so the fix cannot be a lossy fuzzy widening.\n4. PASS: a regression test naming this defect exists in gitreins (tests/), passes, and is named in gitreins' gate pytest arm; quote the collected count and the arm line.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:21:07.99723+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T12:21:07.99723+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
