 to this, and the row then stays open while the work is verifiably done (AUG-121 was re-armed with a compact $PWD/$HOME PATH form as the workaround). Fix belongs in gitreins engine/gate.py, not in auger.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1. PASS: the recorded verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json (task AUG-121, commit ab10427290d8, 9 items whose status is PASS for all nine) must make engine.gate.verdict_is_passing return True; reproduce with PYTHONPATH=<gitreins site-packages> python3 -c 'import json;from engine.gate import check_coverage as cc, verdict_is_passing as vp;v=json.load(open(\".gitreins/history/2026-11-11/9c1182c6/verdict.json\"));c=cc(v,v[\"task_criteria\"]);print(len(c.graded),len(c.ungraded),vp(v,v[\"task_criteria\"]))' -> pre-fix prints 0 6 False; post-fix must print 6 0 True.\n2. PASS: the fix is not 'always pass': a temp copy of that verdict with items[2].status set to FAIL must yield check_coverage(...).failing == 1 and verdict_is_passing False (one-field mutation, printed counts).\n3. PASS: matching stays strict: an item whose criterion text is truncated to its first 30 characters must still be ungraded (fixture prints ungraded == 1), so the fix cannot be a lossy fuzzy widening.\n4. PASS: a regression test naming this defect exists in gitreins (tests/), passes, and is named in gitreins' gate pytest arm; quote the collected count and the arm line.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:21:07.99723+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T01:11:57.423655+00:00", "foreman_note": "SECOND MEASURED OCCURRENCE 2026-11-12 (judge run 857786cf, task AUG-126 @62716e8). tier1 fully green: bash tests/gate.sh -> GATE PASS, 722 passed / 2 skipped in 892.48s, LIVE ARMS ran 2 / skipped 0. tier2 returned all six given items PASS plus four derived items PASS, and the verdict still persisted passed=false because coverage marked exactly ONE criterion ungraded: the task's criterion 6, whose text carried a long chr()-literal list. The evaluator echoed that criterion as \"assert t == [...]\" (SequenceMatcher ratio 0.7954 against 1.0000 for the other five), and engine/gate.py:check_coverage accepts only exact normalized text or a boundary prefix, so an INTERIOR elision can never match. Workaround proven at the criterion-authoring layer: restate the criterion compactly with no repeated literal blob (assert the set relationship and print counts 6/3, bind the kinds<->XSD equality to a named test), then re-judge the SAME task id. The fix for this row must make an interior elision matchable (token-set or subsequence matching in addition to prefix) with a negative control so it cannot degrade to always-pass. AUG-126's first verdict stays published as instrument evidence.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-165", "title": "[WIRE] Factory wiring: every dispatched worker brief embeds auger spec context --task output", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b45b3b5efcc9a48db2db7116cbf3499c7a3635f9a6c2ad050a58875d5234d919"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "The spec context/assemble verbs exist and passed judged runs (AUG-121/122) but NO factory foreman calls them at build time: briefs are still authored from the row text alone. Wire it: on dispatch, the foreman runs `auger spec context --task <row-id>` against the project spec root and embeds the selected blocks (or the structured unscoped/ambiguous answer with its exclusion reasons) in the worker brief.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "A dispatched brief for a task with spec references contains the context-selected blocks verbatim with byte counts; a task with NO spec references produces a brief WITHOUT an empty context section; an ambiguous/unscoped result surfaces in the tick report rather than silently passing. FAILIF: a foreman dispatches a spec-referencing task whose brief lacks the context blocks.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.498732+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.498732+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
