 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-167", "title": "[VER] Corpus time-travel: query the spec selection as-of a version", "detail": {"fingerprint": "da54b000c7e3da3946268f126cec1f0b9847ac327069d897a4f095678c7a6345"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Blocks carry version/status (active/deprecated/superseded) but selection can only answer for NOW. Add `spec list/assemble --as-of <tag-or-version>`: resolve the active set as of that ref (git-backed corpus history), superseded blocks resolved to their historical successors.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "As-of an earlier tag, a block edited since returns its OLD text and the new one is absent; as-of HEAD equals plain selection byte-for-byte; an invalid ref answers with a structured error and rc != 0. FAILIF: --as-of silently returns current-day content.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.64879+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.64879+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-006", "title": "smoke teardown rmtrees the namespace before checking DELETE status: a 409 orphans the registry row (AUG-117 recurrence)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b5ea41def1006b6c2ada07f78d12fed32889437a431727fd36866c72a48c341e"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured live during the 2026-11-11 review: tests/smoke.sh:62-66 calls auger.delete_namespace(ns, retries=1), then runs shutil.rmtree unconditionally, then inspects the status. On HTTP 409 (substrate lock / non-empty) the directory is destroyed and the mapping survives; the script prints 'teardown skipped'. Both throwaway namespaces from that review are still listed by GET /api/namespaces while only one has a directory on disk. AUG-117 describes this exact failure mode and is marked complete.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: tests/smoke.sh treats 409 like 429 (bounded backoff, re-enter) and does not call shutil.rmtree unless the DELETE returned 200 or 404. PASS: a run of 'bash tests/smoke.sh <ns>' on a substrate holding a sibling suite's lock leaves zero rows in GET /api/namespaces and zero directories under the substrate root — verified by listing both after the run and quoting the two empty results on the row. PASS: the two existing leftovers (auger-smoke-rv2314, auger-smoke-rvsmoke) are removed and the removal quoted. FAIL: any code path where rmtree runs before the status check.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:50.968237+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T00:57:00.39653+00:00", "foreman_note": "pytest proof 2026-11-12T00:33Z: the project's own suite reproduces this — 1 failed, 719 passed, 2 skipped, 3 errors in 919.00s. Failure test_no_test_namespace_survives_the_suite + teardown error both say: DELETE returned 409 {'code':'CONFLICT'} 'Push in flight ... Retry after it completes' while tests/test_auger.py retries only 429 and pytest.fail()s otherwise. Fix must cover both paths: the CLI/substrate helper AND the pytest teardown fixture.\n\nregistry census 2026-11-12T00:41Z: GET /api/namespaces lists 34 test-prefixed rows (32 auger-pytest-*, 2 auger-smoke-*); 32 have directories, 2 are registry-only; oldest dir Nov 3 16:39, newest Nov 11 19:55. Nothing reaps them and auger has no delete verb among its 36 subcommands. Acceptance should include draining this backlog, not only stopping new leaks.", "capability_tags": ["teardown", "duckbrain", "smoke", "regression"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
